+A structurally DIFFERENT compressor from the oracle: per-block int8 quantization
+(8 bits/element with an absmax scale) plus the same feedback accumulator. It is a
+valid, unbiased error-feedback compressor, so it passes the whole correctness
+suite — proving the verifier is not oracle-code-matching — but it moves ~8x more
+bytes than the 1-bit oracle (int8 payload ~= numel bytes vs numel/8), so it earns a
+smaller-but-positive byte ratio (~4x over the full-fp32 baseline). Oracle-mode scoring confirms
+baseline2 > 1.0 and oracle > baseline2 in a scoring run.
 """
 
